# RISC0 v1.2.1 Struct Patterns

## Context
- When working with RISC0 v1.2.1 structs
- When creating or modifying Receipt, ReceiptMetadata, SuccinctReceipt, or MerkleProof instances
- When handling proof generation and verification

## Requirements
- Use public API types from crate root:
  ```rust
  use risc0_zkvm::{
      Receipt,
      ReceiptMetadata,
      Digest,
      InnerReceipt,
      VerifierContext,
  };
  ```

### Receipt Creation
- Create receipts using public constructors:
  - Use `Receipt::new()` for receipt creation
  - Use `ReceiptMetadata { verifier_parameters }` for metadata
  - Access fields directly (e.g., `receipt.journal`, `receipt.metadata`)

### Receipt Handling
- Handle receipt variants properly:
  ```rust
  match &receipt.inner {
      InnerReceipt::Succinct(sr) => {
          // Handle succinct receipt
      }
      InnerReceipt::Composite(cr) => {
          // Convert to succinct using prover
          let sr = prover.composite_to_succinct(cr)?;
      }
      _ => {
          // Handle other variants
      }
  }
  ```

### Dev Mode Receipts
- Handle dev mode receipts appropriately:
  ```rust
  if option_env!("RISC0_DEV_MODE").is_some() {
      // Create mock receipt
      Receipt::new(
          InnerReceipt::Fake(mock_data),
          journal_bytes
      )
  }
  ```

## Examples

<example>
// Good: Complete receipt handling
use risc0_zkvm::{Receipt, InnerReceipt, Digest, ReceiptMetadata};

fn process_receipt(receipt: &Receipt, prover: &impl ProverServer) -> Result<Vec<u8>> {
    // Access metadata directly
    let metadata = &receipt.metadata;
    
    // Handle receipt variants
    match &receipt.inner {
        InnerReceipt::Succinct(sr) => {
            // Process succinct receipt
            Ok(sr.get_seal_bytes().to_vec())
        }
        InnerReceipt::Composite(cr) => {
            // Convert to succinct
            let sr = prover.composite_to_succinct(cr)?;
            Ok(sr.get_seal_bytes().to_vec())
        }
        _ => Err(anyhow::anyhow!("Unexpected receipt type"))
    }
}
</example>

<example>
// Good: Dev mode receipt creation
fn create_dev_receipt(claim: ReceiptClaim, journal: Vec<u8>) -> Receipt {
    Receipt::new(
        InnerReceipt::Fake(FakeReceipt {
            claim: MaybePruned::Value(claim),
        }),
        journal
    )
}
</example>

<example type="invalid">
// Bad: Using private types or methods
use risc0_zkvm::host::receipt::ReceiptImpl;  // Wrong: private module

fn create_receipt() -> Receipt {
    ReceiptImpl::new()  // Wrong: using private type
}
</example>

<example type="invalid">
// Bad: Missing variant handling
fn process_unsafe(receipt: Receipt) -> Vec<u8> {
    match receipt.inner {
        InnerReceipt::Succinct(sr) => sr.get_seal_bytes(),
        // Wrong: missing variants
    }
}
</example>

## Critical Notes
<critical>
- ALWAYS use public API types from crate root
- NEVER use private modules or types
- Handle ALL receipt variants
- Use proper error handling
- Follow dev mode patterns when needed
- Maintain proper ownership and borrowing
</critical> 